  "live_records": {
    "q-96861": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96861",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.9362$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ | $\\,0.9382\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ | $\\,0.9495\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9573\\,$ | $\\,0.9582\\,$ | $\\,0.9591\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.9362$ lies between. These numbers are $0.9357$ and $0.9370.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.9357 & <0.9362<0.9370\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.52) & <Φ(z)<Φ(1.53).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{1.52+1.53}{2}=1.525.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
