    "q-328457": {
      "dom_id": "step-q328457",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9608\\,$ | $\\,0.9616\\,$ | $\\,0.9625\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.9686\\,$ | $\\,0.9693\\,$ | $\\,0.9699\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.9750\\,$ | $\\,0.9756\\,$ | $\\,0.9761\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.9620$ using interval bisection and the above table.\n\n$z≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.9620$ lies between. These numbers are $0.9616$ and $0.9625.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.9616 & <0.9620<0.9625\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.77) & <Φ(z)<Φ(1.78).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{1.77+1.78}{2}=1.775.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
