    "q-276188": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276188",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0735\\,$ | $\\,0.0721\\,$ | $\\,0.0708\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0885\\,$ | $\\,0.0869\\,$ | $\\,0.0853\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1056\\,$ | $\\,0.1038\\,$ | $\\,0.1020\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.0860$ using interval bisection and the above table\n\n$z≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.0860$ lies between. These numbers are $0.0869$ and $0.0885.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.0853 & <0.0860<0.0869\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.37) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-1.36).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{-1.37+(-1.36)}{2}=-1.365.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
