    "q-328302": {
      "dom_id": "step-q328302",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.9864\\,$ | $\\,0.9868\\,$ | $\\,0.9871\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.9896\\,$ | $\\,0.9898\\,$ | $\\,0.9901\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9920\\,$ | $\\,0.9922\\,$ | $\\,0.9925\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.9897$ using interval bisection and the above table.\n\n$z≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.9897$ lies between. These numbers are $0.9896$ and $0.9898.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.9896 & <0.9897<0.9898\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(2.31) & <Φ(z)<Φ(2.32).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{2.31+2.32}{2}=2.315.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
