    "q-96941": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96941",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.85.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.85 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.85\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.85).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.85,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.85\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=1.0364.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.85)=1.0364.\n$$",
