    "q-328464": {
      "dom_id": "step-q328464",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.45.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.15$ | $0.20$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.35$ | $0.40$ | $0.45$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ | $\\,-0.5244\\,$ | $\\,-0.3853\\,$ | $\\,-0.2533\\,$ | $\\,-0.1257\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.45 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.45).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.45,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.45\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=-0.1257.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.45)=-0.1257.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
