    "q-328477": {
      "dom_id": "step-q328477",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z>z)=0.025.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.025 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.025 \\\\ 1-Φ(z) & =0.025 \\\\ Φ(z) & =1-0.025 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.975\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.975).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.975,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.975\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=1.96.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.975)=1.96.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
