    "q-328473": {
      "dom_id": "step-q328473",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.05.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.6449)=0.95.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 1.6449)=1-0.95=0.05.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.6449)=0.05.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14263990/assets/904334524aa2468be90f917d2905b07cea091533337584d0bf89c286db079b65.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.6449) & =0.05 \\\\ P(Z\\le -1.6449) & =0.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-1.6449.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
